title The box held two of my own laps
prompt fleet baton, PATCHOULI seat -- open the round, reds first in my own lane
rota lap 4643, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; care and flow. The happy zone and the thin edge read the recovered work exactly: the runner's stop advice is a CONTRACT with an operator, and the control that landed proves the answerer honors it -- said once, latency named, misread named, two lines printed with the pid it was handed -- rather than standing the whole thing up and poking one end. The mutation leg is that page's thin edge: strip the latency sentence and watch the reading fall.
think Opened clean at 785f45f088, no drain files, and launched the cold pass detached so the runner named its own transcript.
think Reds first pointed at my own backlog rather than at code: stash_record refused at unlanded=2 and both records were mine, killed mid-send this morning. My own prior lap had ALREADY named them and gone forward. Reading them back out is the repair the guard exists to ask for.
think The 100007 lap was whole and unsuperseded -- I checked drift rather than assuming, and git diff between the stash's base d34f4307c1 and HEAD reported nothing on all three files, so taking the stash's versions could lose nothing.
think The 102212 lap was the opposite case: real reasoning, superseded code. Its own page names bind-to-zero as the move that frees the window, and bind-to-zero is what landed at 105415. So the record lands and the repair does not.
think A banner rather than an edit, because the page is dated testimony. Status moved from Landed to Testimony, and the erratum sorts its findings into three retired and four standing.
think Then I nearly shipped a banner claim I had not measured. It read "six still stand inside the ephemeral range" from the elder page's prose; running the grep answered SEVEN files holding THIRTEEN constants. Measurement beats memory, including memory of a page written three hours ago by me.
obs MY OWN BREACH, and it is the third firing of this clause on this seat today. I took the three tool files out of the stash while the cold pass was still running FROM standing_equipment_run.sh. That spoils the verdict at best -- the runner digests the tree at open and close -- and at worst a live sh reads a moved byte offset in a script that grew seventeen lines in its middle. The hot pass is this lap's only honest roster reading, and I say so rather than quoting a cold green.
obs THE STOP PROVED ITSELF ON THE WAY OUT. I stopped the spoiled pass through fleet_call.sh --pattern, reading first and signaling second: 9 candidates, 1 sent, 6 peers refused by working directory, 1 self, 1 unreadable. The pass did not die at the signal. It died minutes later, after the guard in flight returned, and its transcript carries no run_verdict line at all -- which is precisely the sentence the recovered stop_line() exists to tell an operator, confirmed on metal by the lap that landed it.
obs No REDS row booked, and the instrument said so rather than the card: reds_pin_capacity reads rows_that_fit=0 with pin_foldable_rows=1, and that one foldable row is a peer's BOOKED %710 from this morning. Folding a peer's row to buy myself space is spending their shelf on my room.
obs The gate closed: stash_record reads records=33 unlanded=0 verdict=ok. The other drawer stands where it stood -- orphans=37, reported and never gated, and 33 of those are fold shelves rather than laps.
